feedback). Production PlayerManaUI.cs in the working tree already contains the previously-flagged fix (capturing the fill Image's actual color in OnEnable instead of a hardcoded white default). I added one new regression test, PlayerManaUI_RevertsToActualFillImageColor_NotHardcodedDefault, that sets the Image's color to a non-default blue (simulating the scene's actual m_Color) before enabling PlayerManaUI, then asserts the denied-flash correctly reverts to that captured blue rather than a hardcoded default. This closes the gap the validator identified: prior tests only used AddComponent<Image>()'s default white color, which coincidentally matched the hardcoded field-initializer default and could not distinguish a real fix from the original bug. No production code was modified.\",\"claimed_changed_paths\":[\"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Tests/PlayerManaPlayModeTests.cs\"],\"test_cases_added_or_updated\":[\"PlayerManaUI_RevertsToActualFillImageColor_NotHardcodedDefault (new, regression-only, targets prior validator blocking finding re: hardcoded normalColor default vs scene-authored fill Image color)\"],\"blockers\":[],\"known_limitations\":[\"No tests were executed; this is static test authorship only, per policy (no Unity/build/test execution performed).\",\"The new test uses an in-memory Image component with a manually assigned color to simulate the scene's blue-tinted fill Image; it does not open the committed DoorPrototype.unity scene to read the actual authored m_Color value, since committed-scene conformance testing was outside this task's file-write scope.\",\"PlayerManaUI.cs and PlayerMana.cs are read-only to this role; the code already reflects the fix the prior validator pass required, but that was not verified by re-running any suite.\",\"Human Play Mode / visual verification of the actual blue mana-fill indicator flashing and reverting correctly in the real DoorPrototype scene is still required, since no automated test opens or inspects that committed scene's Image color.\"],\"proposed_unity_test_scope\":\"Play Mode behavior tests (UnityTest coroutines) plus one pure/component reflection-based test, all using freshly constructed in-memory GameObjects (PlayerMana, PlayerManaUI, Image) rather than the committed DoorPrototype.unity scene. Suite: NoSafeCircle.DoorPrototype.Tests / PlayerManaPlayModeTests via Unity Test Runner (Play Mode), filter class=NoSafeCircle.DoorPrototype.Tests.PlayerManaPlayModeTests. No scene, prefab, or ScriptableObject asset is opened or saved; non-mutation invariant is preserved by construction (all objects are created and destroyed within each test's SetUp/TearDown or try/finally block).\"}","structured_output":{"summary":"The existing PlayerManaPlayModeTests.cs already covered AC-001 (ResetMana), AC-002 (CastDenied event + UI flash), AC-003 (public API surface lock), and VAL-002/VAL-003 (readable low-mana feedback). Production PlayerManaUI.cs in the working tree already contains the previously-flagged fix (capturing the fill Image's actual color in OnEnable instead of a hardcoded white default). I added one new regression test, PlayerManaUI_RevertsToActualFillImageColor_NotHardcodedDefault, that sets the Image's color to a non-default blue (simulating the scene's actual m_Color) before enabling PlayerManaUI, then asserts the denied-flash correctly reverts to that captured blue rather than a hardcoded default. This closes the gap the validator identified: prior tests only used AddComponent<Image>()'s default white color, which coincidentally matched the hardcoded field-initializer default and could not distinguish a real fix from the original bug. No production code was modified.","claimed_changed_paths":["Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Tests/PlayerManaPlayModeTests.cs"],"test_cases_added_or_updated":["PlayerManaUI_RevertsToActualFillImageColor_NotHardcodedDefault (new, regression-only, targets prior validator blocking finding re: hardcoded normalColor default vs scene-authored fill Image color)"],"blockers":[],"known_limitations":["No tests were executed; this is static test authorship only, per policy (no Unity/build/test execution performed).","The new test uses an in-memory Image component with a manually assigned color to simulate the scene's blue-tinted fill Image; it does not open the committed DoorPrototype.unity scene to read the actual authored m_Color value, since committed-scene conformance testing was outside this task's file-write scope.","PlayerManaUI.cs and PlayerMana.cs are read-only to this role; the code already reflects the fix the prior validator pass required, but that was not verified by re-running any suite.","Human Play Mode / visual verification of the actual blue mana-fill indicator flashing and reverting correctly in the real DoorPrototype scene is still required, since no automated test opens or inspects that committed scene's Image color."],"proposed_unity_test_scope":"Play Mode behavior tests (UnityTest coroutines) plus one pure/component reflection-based test, all using freshly constructed in-memory GameObjects (PlayerMana, PlayerManaUI, Image) rather than the committed DoorPrototype.unity scene. Suite: NoSafeCircle.DoorPrototype.Tests / PlayerManaPlayModeTests via Unity Test Runner (Play Mode), filter class=NoSafeCircle.DoorPrototype.Tests.PlayerManaPlayModeTests. No scene, prefab, or ScriptableObject asset is opened or saved; non-mutation invariant is preserved by construction (all objects are created and destroyed within each test's SetUp/TearDown or try/finally block)."},"ttft_ms":2052,"ttft_stream_ms":1476,"time_to_request_ms":28,"type":"result","duration_ms":52301,"uuid":"72f941fc-0252-43ed-9f3d-1d5daf09dcca"}
